-- src:164 | COVID-19 affected claimant: a person is a COVID-19 affected claimant in relation to a claim for parental leave pay for a child if:
-- src:165 | (a) either:
-- src:166 | (i) the child is or was born between 22 March 2020 and 31 March 2021; or
-- src:167 | (ii) if the claim is made before the child’s birth—the child’s expected date of birth is during that period; and
-- src:168 | (b) the person must satisfy the work test to be eligible for parental leave pay; and
-- src:169 | (c) the Secretary is satisfied that any of the following circumstances apply in relation to the person:
-- src:170 | (i) the person became unemployed as a result of the adverse effects of the coronavirus known as COVID-19;
-- src:171 | (ii) the person’s working hours were reduced (including to zero) as a result of the adverse effects of the coronavirus known as COVID-19;
-- src:172 | (iii) a business that the person, or an entity that is controlled by the person, carries on for profit and for which the person performs work was suspended, or suffered a reduction in turnover, as a result of the adverse effects of the coronavirus known as COVID-19; and
-- src:173 | (d) as a result of that circumstance applying in relation to the person, the person would not satisfy the work test if the person’s work test period were the period under section 33.
@ref s 6, COVID-19 affected claimant (src:164-173)
`the Dictionary entry for COVID-19 affected claimant` MEANS `Dictionary entry` OF "COVID-19 affected claimant", DefinedInTheDictionary, "", 164

