GIVEN term IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE `Dictionary entry`
`the entry in the table for` MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN e YIELD e's term EQUALS term) `the Dictionary entries`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN e FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST e

§ `Part 2 -- the entries that define a term`

-- src:142 | born prematurely: a child is born prematurely if, at the time of the child’s delivery, the child’s period of gestation is less than 37 weeks.
@ref s 6, born prematurely: a child is born prematurely if, at the time of the child's delivery, the period of gestation is less than 37 weeks (src:142-142)
GIVEN `weeks of gestation at the time of the child's delivery` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a child is born prematurely` MEANS
    JUST (`the period of gestation is less than 37 weeks` `weeks of gestation at the time of the child's delivery`)

-- src:325 | stillborn, in relation to a child, means a child:
-- src:326 | (a) who weighs at least 400 grams at delivery or whose period of gestation was at least 20 weeks; and
-- src:327 | (b) who has not breathed since delivery; and
-- src:328 | (c) whose heart has not beaten since delivery.
@ref s 6, stillborn: a child who weighs at least 400 grams or whose gestation was at least 20 weeks, has not breathed and whose heart has not beaten since delivery (src:325-328)
GIVEN `weight at delivery in grams` IS A NUMBER
      `weeks of gestation` IS A NUMBER
      `the child has breathed since delivery` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child's heart has beaten since delivery` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a child is stillborn` MEANS
    JUST (        `the child weighed at least 400 grams or the gestation was at least 20 weeks` `weight at delivery in grams` `weeks of gestation`
          AND (NOT `the child has breathed since delivery`)
          AND (NOT `the child's heart has beaten since delivery`))

-- src:268 | parent:
-- src:269 | (a) when used in relation to a child who has been adopted—means an adoptive parent of the child; and
-- src:270 | (b) when used in relation to a child born because of the carrying out of an artificial conception procedure—means a person who is a parent of the child under section 60H of the Family Law Act 1975; and
-- src:271 | (c) when used in relation to a child born because of a surrogacy arrangement—includes a person who is a parent of the child under section 60HB of the Family Law Act 1975.
@ref s 6, parent: for an adopted child an adoptive parent; for a child born because of an artificial conception procedure a parent under section 60H of the Family Law Act 1975; for a child born because of a surrogacy arrangement includes a parent under section 60HB (src:268-271)
GIVEN relationship IS A `The parental relationship`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the person is a parent of the child under the Dictionary` MEANS
    BRANCH IF relationship's `the child was adopted`
           THEN JUST (relationship's `the person is an adoptive parent of the child`)
           IF relationship's `the child was born because of an artificial conception procedure`
           THEN JUST (relationship's `the person is a parent of the child under section 60H of the Family Law Act 1975`)
           IF relationship's `the child was born because of a surrogacy arrangement` AND relationship's `the person is a parent of the child under section 60HB of the Family Law Act 1975`
           THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:268 | parent:
-- src:269 | (a) when used in relation to a child who has been adopted—means an adoptive parent of the child; and
-- src:270 | (b) when used in relation to a child born because of the carrying out of an artificial conception procedure—means a person who is a parent of the child under section 60H of the Family Law Act 1975; and
-- src:271 | (c) when used in relation to a child born because of a surrogacy arrangement—includes a person who is a parent of the child under section 60HB of the Family Law Act 1975.
@ref s 6, parent: where the Dictionary gives no meaning the person's own answer is taken, the ordinary sense of the word (src:268-271)
GIVEN relationship IS A `The parental relationship`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is a parent of the child, taking the ordinary sense where the Dictionary gives none` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person is a parent of the child under the Dictionary` relationship
    WHEN JUST answer THEN answer
    WHEN NOTHING THEN relationship's `the person is a parent of the child in the ordinary sense`

DECLARE `Kind of occupation` IS ONE OF
    Profession
    Trade
    Employment
    Vocation
    Calling
    `Occupation as an employee`
    `Any other occupation`

-- src:143 | business includes any profession, trade, employment, vocation or calling, but does not include occupation as an employee.
@ref s 6, business includes any profession, trade, employment, vocation or calling, but does not include occupation as an employee (src:143-143)
GIVEN occupation IS A `Kind of occupation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an occupation is a business` MEANS
    CONSIDER occupation
    WHEN `Occupation as an employee` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `Any other occupation` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `Kind of party` IS ONE OF
    `A natural person`
    `A body corporate`
    `A body of the fourth kind in the list`
    `A partnership`
    `Any other unincorporated association or body of persons`
    `A trust`
    `Any other kind of party`

-- src:199 | entity means any of the following:
-- src:200 | (a) a natural person;
-- src:201 | (b) a body corporate;
-- src:202 | (c) a body politic;
-- src:203 | (d) a partnership;
-- src:204 | (e) any other unincorporated association or body of persons;
-- src:205 | (f) a trust.
@ref s 6, entity (src:199-205)
GIVEN party IS A `Kind of party`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a party is an entity` MEANS
    CONSIDER party
    WHEN `Any other kind of party` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:149 | claim means a PPL claim or special PPL claim for parental leave pay for a child.
@ref s 6, claim means a PPL claim or special PPL claim for parental leave pay for a child (src:149-149)
GIVEN `the request is a PPL claim for parental leave pay for a child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is a special PPL claim for parental leave pay for a child` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a request is a claim` MEANS
    JUST (`the request is a PPL claim for parental leave pay for a child` OR `the request is a special PPL claim for parental leave pay for a child`)

-- src:150 | claimant means a person who is a PPL claimant or special PPL claimant.
@ref s 6, claimant means a person who is a PPL claimant or special PPL claimant (src:150-150)
GIVEN `the person is a PPL claimant` IS A BOOLEAN, `the person is a special PPL claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a person is a claimant` MEANS
    JUST (`the person is a PPL claimant` OR `the person is a special PPL claimant`)

-- src:292 | PPL claimant means a person who has made an effective PPL claim for parental leave pay for a child.
@ref s 6, PPL claimant means a person who has made an effective PPL claim for parental leave pay for a child (src:292-292)
GIVEN `the person has made an effective PPL claim for parental leave pay for the child` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a person is a PPL claimant` MEANS
    JUST `the person has made an effective PPL claim for parental leave pay for the child`

-- src:324 | special PPL claimant means a person who has made an effective special PPL claim for parental leave pay for a child for which another person has made a PPL claim.
@ref s 6, special PPL claimant means a person who has made an effective special PPL claim for a child for which another person has made a PPL claim (src:324-324)
GIVEN `the person has made an effective special PPL claim for parental leave pay for the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another person has made a PPL claim for the child` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a person is a special PPL claimant` MEANS
    JUST (`the person has made an effective special PPL claim for parental leave pay for the child` AND `another person has made a PPL claim for the child`)

-- src:183 | effective claim means a claim that is made in accordance with Part 2-4.
@ref s 6, effective claim means a claim that is made in accordance with Part 2-4 (src:183-183)
GIVEN `the request is a claim` IS A BOOLEAN, `the claim is made in accordance with Part 2-4` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a claim is an effective claim` MEANS
    JUST (`the request is a claim` AND `the claim is made in accordance with Part 2-4`)

-- src:159 | conditional eligibility determination means a determination of a kind mentioned in paragraph 13(6)(b) or 14(4)(b).
@ref s 6, conditional eligibility determination means a determination of a kind mentioned in paragraph 13(6)(b) or 14(4)(b) (src:159-159)
GIVEN `the determination is of the kind mentioned in paragraph 13(6)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the determination is of the kind mentioned in paragraph 14(4)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a determination is a conditional eligibility determination` MEANS
    JUST (`the determination is of the kind mentioned in paragraph 13(6)(b)` OR `the determination is of the kind mentioned in paragraph 14(4)(b)`)

-- src:274 | payability determination means a determination made under section 13 or 14 that parental leave pay is, or is not, payable to a person for a child.
@ref s 6, payability determination means a determination made under section 13 or 14 that parental leave pay is, or is not, payable to a person for a child (src:274-274)
GIVEN `the determination is made under section 13` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the determination is made under section 14` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the determination says that parental leave pay is, or is not, payable to a person for a child` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a determination is a payability determination` MEANS
    JUST ((`the determination is made under section 13` OR `the determination is made under section 14`) AND `the determination says that parental leave pay is, or is not, payable to a person for a child`)

-- src:227 | has not previously satisfied the work and income tests: a person has not previously satisfied the work and income tests in relation to a child if both of the following apply:
-- src:228 | (a) no payability determination is in force that parental leave pay is payable to the person in relation to the child;
-- src:229 | (b) no conditional eligibility determination is in force that relates to the person and child.
@ref s 6, has not previously satisfied the work and income tests: no payability determination and no conditional eligibility determination is in force (src:227-229)
GIVEN `a payability determination that parental leave pay is payable to the person in relation to the child is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a conditional eligibility determination that relates to the person and child is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a person has not previously satisfied the work and income tests in relation to a child` MEANS
    JUST (    (NOT `a payability determination that parental leave pay is payable to the person in relation to the child is in force`)
          AND (NOT `a conditional eligibility determination that relates to the person and child is in force`))

-- src:206 | exceptional circumstances: a claim is made in exceptional circumstances if it is made by a person who satisfies:
-- src:207 | (a) paragraph 54(1)(g) (which deals with PPL claims); or
-- src:208 | (b) paragraph 54(2)(b) (which deals with special PPL claims).
@ref s 6, exceptional circumstances: a claim is made in exceptional circumstances if made by a person who satisfies paragraph 54(1)(g) or 54(2)(b) (src:206-208)
GIVEN `the person satisfies paragraph 54(1)(g), which deals with PPL claims` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person satisfies paragraph 54(2)(b), which deals with special PPL claims` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a claim is made in exceptional circumstances` MEANS
    JUST (`the person satisfies paragraph 54(1)(g), which deals with PPL claims` OR `the person satisfies paragraph 54(2)(b), which deals with special PPL claims`)

-- src:164 | COVID-19 affected claimant: a person is a COVID-19 affected claimant in relation to a claim for parental leave pay for a child if:
-- src:165 | (a) either:
-- src:166 | (i) the child is or was born between 22 March 2020 and 31 March 2021; or
-- src:167 | (ii) if the claim is made before the child’s birth—the child’s expected date of birth is during that period; and
-- src:168 | (b) the person must satisfy the work test to be eligible for parental leave pay; and
-- src:169 | (c) the Secretary is satisfied that any of the following circumstances apply in relation to the person:
-- src:170 | (i) the person became unemployed as a result of the adverse effects of the coronavirus known as COVID-19;
-- src:171 | (ii) the person’s working hours were reduced (including to zero) as a result of the adverse effects of the coronavirus known as COVID-19;
-- src:172 | (iii) a business that the person, or an entity that is controlled by the person, carries on for profit and for which the person performs work was suspended, or suffered a reduction in turnover, as a result of the adverse effects of the coronavirus known as COVID-19; and
-- src:173 | (d) as a result of that circumstance applying in relation to the person, the person would not satisfy the work test if the person’s work test period were the period under section 33.
@ref s 6, COVID-19 affected claimant: the child is born, or is expected to be born, between 22 March 2020 and 31 March 2021; the work test applies; a circumstance applies; the person would not satisfy the work test with the usual period (src:164-173)
GIVEN `the child's date of birth, if the child has been born` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the claim is made before the child's birth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child's expected date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the person must satisfy the work test to be eligible for parental leave pay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person became unemployed as a result of the adverse effects of COVID-19` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's working hours were reduced as a result of the adverse effects of COVID-19` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a business the person or an entity they control carries on for profit was suspended or suffered a reduction in turnover as a result of COVID-19` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person would not satisfy the work test if the work test period were the period under section 33 because of that circumstance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a person is a COVID-19 affected claimant` MEANS
    JUST (        (`the child was born in the period` OR (`the claim is made before the child's birth` AND `a day is between 22 March 2020 and 31 March 2021` `the child's expected date of birth`))
          AND `the person must satisfy the work test to be eligible for parental leave pay`
          AND (   `the person became unemployed as a result of the adverse effects of COVID-19`
               OR `the person's working hours were reduced as a result of the adverse effects of COVID-19`
               OR `a business the person or an entity they control carries on for profit was suspended or suffered a reduction in turnover as a result of COVID-19`)
          AND `the person would not satisfy the work test if the work test period were the period under section 33 because of that circumstance`)
    WHERE
        `the child was born in the period` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the child's date of birth, if the child has been born`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST born THEN `a day is between 22 March 2020 and 31 March 2021` born

-- src:185 | employee has its ordinary meaning and:
-- src:186 | (a) includes a reference to a person who is usually such an employee; and
-- src:187 | (b) does not include a person on a vocational placement.
@ref s 6, employee has its ordinary meaning, includes a person usually such an employee, and does not include a person on a vocational placement (src:185-187)
GIVEN `the person is an employee in the ordinary sense` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is usually such an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is on a vocational placement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a person is an employee` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the person is on a vocational placement` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the person is an employee in the ordinary sense` OR `the person is usually such an employee` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:188 | employer has its ordinary meaning and includes a reference to a person who is usually such an employer.
@ref s 6, employer has its ordinary meaning and includes a person who is usually such an employer (src:188-188)
GIVEN `the person is an employer in the ordinary sense` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is usually such an employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a person is an employer` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the person is an employer in the ordinary sense` OR `the person is usually such an employer` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:348 | vocational placement means a placement that is:
-- src:349 | (a) undertaken with an employer for which a person is not entitled to be paid any remuneration; and
-- src:350 | (b) undertaken as a requirement of an education or training course; and
-- src:351 | (c) authorised under a law or an administrative arrangement of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory.
@ref s 6, vocational placement means a placement undertaken with an employer without entitlement to remuneration, as a requirement of an education or training course, and authorised under a law or administrative arrangement (src:348-351)
GIVEN `undertaken with an employer for which the person is not entitled to be paid any remuneration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `undertaken as a requirement of an education or training course` IS A BOOLEAN
      `authorised under a law or an administrative arrangement of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a placement is a vocational placement` MEANS
    JUST (        `undertaken with an employer for which the person is not entitled to be paid any remuneration`
          AND `undertaken as a requirement of an education or training course`
          AND `authorised under a law or an administrative arrangement of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory`)

DECLARE `Kind of instrument` IS ONE OF
    `This Act as made and amended`
    `The PPL rules`
    `The regulations`
    `Any other instrument`

-- src:340 | this Act includes the PPL rules and the regulations.
@ref s 6, this Act includes the PPL rules and the regulations (src:340-340)
GIVEN instrument IS A `Kind of instrument`
